# No Backwards Compatibility (Pre-Release)

This app is **unreleased**. There are no external consumers, saved data, or
bookmarked URLs to protect. **Never** spend effort on backwards compatibility.

- Do **not** add redirects, aliases, deprecation shims, re-exports, adapters,
  fallbacks, or "legacy" code paths to keep old behavior working.
- Do **not** keep old fields, routes, functions, config keys, or APIs "just in
  case." Delete them outright and update every call site.
- Do **not** version APIs/schemas or offer migration paths for old formats.
- Prefer the clean, correct design and change all usages in place — even for
  breaking changes to URLs, storage keys, data shapes, or public signatures.
- Don't ask whether to preserve old behavior; assume the answer is no.

> Removed after our first release.
